      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never loading it into the Hub\u0027s environment in the first place**. Here\u0027s how it works, according to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n1. **Secrets are loaded externally**: A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n2. **Key is injected only into child processes**: The key is injected directly into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start \u2014 not into the Hub\u0027s own process environment.\n\n3. **Hub\u0027s environment stays clean**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated, so a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables.\n\n4. **Short-lived credential exposure**: The key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API, minimizing the attack surface.\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised, the credential is not available within it \u2014 it only exists within the isolated child processes that need it.",
